.\" man/wwwr.1 -- manual page for the bin/wwwr operational CLI.
.\" View with:  man ./man/wwwr.1     Install: see FILES.
.TH WWWR 1 "2026-09-02" "wwworkremote/core" "WWWorkRemote Manual"
.SH NAME
wwwr \- WWWorkRemote operational CLI: pipeline health, postings, transitions, prep packs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bin/wwwr
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B bin/wwwr
.RB [ --help | -h ]
.RB [ help
.IR command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wwwr
is the shell-side pipeline and data control surface for a single-user WWWorkRemote
install. It answers "what is the state of the pipeline / a specific posting" and drives
operator transitions, job matching, and interview-prep generation without a
.B bin/rails runner
one-liner. All reads and writes act against the one local user.
.PP
Service lifecycle management (web, SolidQueue workers, launchd supervision) is handled
by companion tools
.BR bin/wwwr-ctl ,
.BR bin/wwwr-jobs ,
and
.BR bin/wwwr-web .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print a pipeline health summary: job-posting and source counts, pending
documents, whether pipelines are paused, the SolidQueue error rate, and the
oldest unclaimed job.
.TP
.BI "postings " "[filters]"
List up to 20 postings matching the given filters. With no match, says so.
.TP
.BI "transition " "<id> <event>"
Apply one lifecycle or pipeline event to a posting and record it against the
user's tracked record. Illegal transitions are reported, never raised.
.TP
.BI "match " "<id> --source=<name> [--escalate]"
Return the job-fit score and analysis for a posting. Reads an existing
analysis for free;
.B --escalate
runs a fresh LLM scan.
.B --source
is required for attribution logging. See
.IR docs/agents/interop.md .
.TP
.BI "interview-prep " "<id> [--regenerate] [--spoken] [--export[=<role>]]"
Print or generate the interview prep pack for a posting. Two versions, same
content: a human version and a read-aloud version for text-to-speech.
.TP
.BI "help " "[command]"
With a command, print its detailed help. Without, print the usage summary.
.B --help
and
.B -h
are aliases for the summary.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS postings filters
.TP
.BI --company= NAME
Match the company name (substring).
.TP
.BI --source-id= ID
Match the ingestion source.
.TP
.BI --role-family= FAMILY
Match the role family.
.TP
.BI --location= LOCATION
Match the location string.
.TP
.B --remote
Only remote postings.
.TP
.B --contract
Only contract / temp postings.
.SS transition events
.B favorite\fR, \fBapply\fR, \fBinterview\fR, \fBoffer\fR, \fBreject\fR, \fBignore\fR, \fBarchive
(the exact list is printed by
.BR "bin/wwwr --help" ).
.SS interview-prep flags
.TP
.B (no flags)
Print the stored human pack; generate one if none exists.
.TP
.B --regenerate
Force a fresh generation. Rewrites both the human and the read-aloud version.
.TP
.B --spoken
Print the read-aloud version instead of the human one.
.TP
.B --export
Write
.B pack.md
and
.B pack.spoken.md
to
.IR ~/ai/outbox/wwwr/interview-prep/<role>/ .
The read-aloud file gains discovery frontmatter
.RB ( "format: read-aloud" ", " kind ", " lang ", " source ", " generated_at )
ahead of the content hints.
.TP
.BI --export= ROLE
Use
.I ROLE
as the subdirectory name instead of the company slug.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I bin/wwwr
The five-line operational CLI shim; logic in
.IR lib/wwwr/cli.rb .
.TP
.I bin/wwwr-ctl ", " bin/wwwr-jobs ", " bin/wwwr-web
Service lifecycle and launchd supervision controllers.
.TP
.I ~/ai/outbox/wwwr/interview-prep/<role>/
Exported prep packs (generated artifacts, outside the repo).
.TP
.I completions/wwwr.bash ", " completions/wwwr.zsh
Shell completion. Install by sourcing
.I completions/wwwr.bash
from
.IR ~/.bashrc ,
or adding
.I completions/
to
.B fpath
before
.B compinit
in
.IR ~/.zshrc .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bin/wwwr-ctl (1),
.BR bin/wwwr-jobs (1),
.BR bin/wwwr-web (1),
.IR docs/agents/bin-scripts.md ,
.IR docs/interview-prep/README.md ,
.IR docs/architecture/interview-prep-tooling.md ,
.IR docs/agents/interop.md
.SH AUTHOR
Mike Hall.
